        "title": "freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via uninitialized progressive tile handling"
      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2026-109676",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-416",
          "name": "Use After Free"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-10-13T13:58:50.614349+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2550539"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in FreeRDP. When a user connects to a malicious Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) server, the server can trigger an invalid smartcard connect operation, leading to a use-after-free vulnerability where previously released memory is accessed. A remote attacker can exploit this issue to cause memory corruption, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution or a Denial of Service (DoS) through an application crash.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "freerdp: FreeRDP 3.0.0-beta1 before 3.32.0 Use-After-Free via Smartcard Connect",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This flaw is rated Important because a malicious RDP peer can trigger memory corruption in the FreeRDP client after the user connects (UI:R), with potential impact beyond a simple crash. Red Hat heap/allocator hardening and ASLR raise exploitation difficulty but do not justify lowering Confidentiality/Integrity/Availability in the base score when corruption is confirmed. This is the highest-severity issue in this FreeRDP set (CVSS 8.8) but remains Important rather than Critical because exploitation requires the user to connect to a malicious RDP server (UI:R).",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
