        "title": "freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via unbounded memory consumption during RDPDR reassembly"
      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2026-110837",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-122",
          "name": "Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-10-14T23:02:39.532885+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2552978"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in FreeRDP. A malicious Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) server can exploit this vulnerability by sending specially crafted MP3 audio data to a connected client. Due to an incorrect buffer size calculation during audio decoding, decoded audio data can be written beyond allocated memory limits, resulting in a heap-based buffer overflow. This flaw allows an attacker to crash the client application, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS).",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap-based buffer overflow during MP3 audio decoding",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This flaw is rated Important because crafted MP3 audio from a malicious RDP server can cause a heap buffer overflow in the client after the user connects (UI:R), with integrity and availability impact and limited confidentiality impact (CVSS 7.1). Decode-path constraints keep Attack Complexity High. Allocator hardening may impede exploitation but does not clear I:H/A:H.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
