        "cve": "CVE-2026-111378",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-770",
          "name": "Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-10-16T01:40:56.515294+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2553907"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in FreeRDP. An unauthenticated remote attacker can cause a Denial of Service (DoS) by exhausting server memory. When processing Network Level Authentication (NLA) connections over Transport Layer Security (TLS), the server misinterprets invalid protocol bytes as an incomplete packet rather than rejecting them. This triggers unbounded receive buffer growth as incoming data is streamed, consuming server memory until the service becomes unresponsive or crashes.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via memory exhaustion in NLA frame parser",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "Red Hat Product Security has rated this vulnerability as having an Important impact because an unauthenticated remote attacker can exhaust server memory prior to authentication without requiring valid user credentials or privileges. While FreeRDP packages in Red Hat Enterprise Linux are primarily utilized for client-side connectivity, server implementations and services utilizing FreeRDP server libraries with Network Level Authentication are exposed to denial of service from unbounded buffer growth. Deployments that solely execute FreeRDP as an outbound client remain unaffected.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
