      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2026-111381",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-787",
          "name": "Out-of-bounds Write"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-10-16T01:41:32.679134+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2553917"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in FreeRDP. This flaw allows arbitrary code execution or a Denial of Service (DoS) when parsing persistent cache files. A local attacker can trigger this vulnerability by tricking a user into loading a maliciously crafted cache file containing oversized image dimensions. This manipulation leads to an integer calculation error and a heap-based buffer overflow, causing memory corruption.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "freerdp: freerdp: Arbitrary code execution via crafted persistent cache file",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "A heap-based buffer overflow was found in FreeRDP's persistent cache v2 parser (persistent_cache_read_entry_v2 in libfreerdp/cache/persistent.c). An integer wraparound in the bitmap size calculation allows a crafted persistent cache v2 file containing oversized width and height values to bypass bounds checks, causing mismatched entry size accounting and fixed 16 KiB reads that corrupt heap memory. A local attacker can exploit this flaw by convincing a user to load a maliciously crafted persistent cache file, resulting in a crash of the FreeRDP client or potential arbitrary code execution in the context of the user running the client. Red Hat rates this flaw as IMPORTANT (CVSS 7.3, CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H), consistent with the upstream Important rating, with exploitation requiring user interaction to load the attacker-supplied cache file. The freerdp package as shipped in Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7, 8, 9, and 10, freerdp and freerdp2 in Red Hat In-Vehicle OS, and freerdp and freerdp2 in Fedora and EPEL are affected, and fixes for these products are being pursued.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
