      {
        "cve": "CVE-2026-111880",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-787",
          "name": "Out-of-bounds Write"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-10-17T19:02:09.270418+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2554625"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in FreeRDP. An out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the server-side NT LAN Manager (NTLM) authentication path can result in a Denial of Service (DoS). When processing authentication messages with hash callbacks enabled, FreeRDP fails to properly validate the Message Integrity Check (MIC) offset. A remote, unauthenticated attacker can exploit this issue by sending a specially crafted authentication message, corrupting heap memory and causing the server to crash.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap out-of-bounds write in NTLM authentication",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This issue is reachable only on FreeRDP server or proxy peers that configure the non-default SspiNtlmHashCallback NTLM hash callback, which is reflected as Attack Complexity: High. An unauthenticated network attacker can cause a fixed 16-byte out-of-bounds heap write, so Integrity and Availability are High; Confidentiality is None. Red Hat rates this Important. Platform safeguards such as ASLR, NX, FORTIFY_SOURCE, and glibc allocator hardening may impede reliable code execution, but they do not prevent the out-of-bounds write or process crash, so the base metrics are unchanged.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
