        "title": "freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap out-of-bounds write in NTLM authentication"
      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2026-114045",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-122",
          "name": "Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-10-21T00:55:40.781083+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2557974"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in FreeRDP. An integer wraparound in rdpsnd_server_select_format() DVI_ADPCM block-alignment arithmetic bypasses validation in the server-side rdpsnd channel. A malicious RDP client can send crafted SNDC_FORMATS PDUs, causing an unbounded heap write during server audio playback that may enable code execution. This issue affects FreeRDP before 3.32.1.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "freerdp: FreeRDP: heap buffer overflow in server rdpsnd via crafted audio formats",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This issue is rated Important because an authenticated RDP client can trigger a heap-based buffer overflow in the FreeRDP server audio (rdpsnd) channel without further user interaction (PR:L, UI:N), with High impact on confidentiality, integrity, and availability. The vulnerable code is in the server-side rdpsnd path shipped when FreeRDP server components (for example freerdp-server / freerdp-shadow-cli) are built and used. Red Hat products that ship FreeRDP with server support before 3.32.1 are affected. Platform hardening such as ASLR, NX, and FORTIFY_SOURCE may make reliable exploitation more difficult but does not remove the underlying memory-corruption risk.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
